@* Inside a popover, which is shadcn's date-picker shape. No width class at all, where
   upstream writes w-auto: there the panel sits inside a Radix positioner that is already
   fit-content, while here the panel IS the positioned element, and a positioned box with
   `width: auto` stretches to the space it is offered — which put the right-hand half of the
   calendar off the edge of the window. A panel that names no width now sizes to its content. For a form field, <DatePicker> around
   <input type="date"> is smaller and brings the OS picker on a phone — reach for this when the
   month has to be visible while choosing. *@
<div class="w-[280px]">
    <Field>
        <FieldLabel For="cal-dp">Delivery date</FieldLabel>
        <PopoverTrigger Target="cal-dp-panel" id="cal-dp" Class="w-full justify-between font-normal">
            <span data-date-label>11 March 2026</span><Icon Name="calendar" Class="opacity-50" />
        </PopoverTrigger>
        <PopoverContent Id="cal-dp-panel" Align="start" Class="p-3">
            <Calendar Name="delivery" Month="@(new DateOnly(2026, 3, 1))"
                      Selected="@(new DateOnly(2026, 3, 11))" Today="@(new DateOnly(2026, 3, 11))" />
        </PopoverContent>
    </Field>
</div>
